#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546100 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f94917e-78d9-52bc-9103-b3aa58254bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546103} {:answer/id #uuid "74e08380-dbb3-5f70-9c7e-611060b429fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546106} {:answer/id #uuid "7a922356-8f4a-52d3-84a0-281bf46f725e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546107} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddfa5c6-05c7-5ea0-a725-59cb12018d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546110} {:answer/id #uuid "bed2a4e2-0193-53a3-a7a0-4253b4a41bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74e08380-dbb3-5f70-9c7e-611060b429fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546106} :answer-field/id #uuid "7df0dce6-cc14-5497-9d94-d12087364d6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4295ba3c-10ba-5642-926e-19c46049c936" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-1)\\cdot (z)+(-2)\\cdot (x)+(3)\\cdot (y),$ where $x=t - 3 s$, $y=- s - t$, $z=- s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =-3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-2)\\cdot (-3)+(3)\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =6 - 3 + 1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "857a1876-c6e3-5505-9faa-9ecd990ae58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546114} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d56532-27b4-5eff-9836-0b6262145a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546121} {:answer/id #uuid "c94708e4-84a0-5302-8628-b7126abcee55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546123} {:answer/id #uuid "d737bd49-5a89-5ae7-8f96-bf16b1e54625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546125} {:answer/id #uuid "fd34d9a4-823a-58a7-9e11-333648863951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3d56532-27b4-5eff-9836-0b6262145a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546121} :answer-field/id #uuid "935c08d8-4b0b-5756-9deb-58e791d8fbfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c95ae4a-2914-518f-a79c-f9b0d943acd0" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-3)\\cdot (x)+(3)\\cdot (y)+(3)\\cdot (z),$ where $x=s + t$, $y=- t + 2 s$, $z=- 3 s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =2, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-3)\\cdot (1)+(3)\\cdot (2)+(3)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-3 + 6 - 9 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0918a1aa-355c-5ba1-bb19-71dd88423a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546096} {:answer/id #uuid "5b02881d-2eac-5e5d-a7ce-9f727da4751b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546102} {:answer/id #uuid "6bceb32a-606e-55f0-9d4f-822db8e38b16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546105} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c4e5e5-aeb5-54f9-ad76-f60621883784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546126} {:answer/id #uuid "efa24f2f-c82a-5669-bf87-fcc404d17ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bceb32a-606e-55f0-9d4f-822db8e38b16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546105} :answer-field/id #uuid "18c30189-b4f2-558c-9b0d-3c32eb3f57b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e641e96-3565-5d21-a6bc-cdd20f093a9f" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-3)\\cdot (y)+(-2)\\cdot (x)+(-2)\\cdot (z),$ where $x=t - 3 s$, $y=- t + 3 s$, $z=2 s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =-3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-2)\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (3)+(-2)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =6 - 9 - 4 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c5921e1-f78d-547f-a005-e59e1e960262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546098} {:answer/id #uuid "415c5fbd-8bd8-5755-abbf-2c7975ac0695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546099} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5a5f44-5875-53a6-ad90-f5f834be8981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546112} {:answer/id #uuid "c5307b2d-4be5-50f6-ae59-623ff7562952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546122} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf1e3a1-337d-59b7-a896-d049ae0219c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5307b2d-4be5-50f6-ae59-623ff7562952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546122} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3244ce3-a8c1-51a5-9032-eb55f4145641" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e3a4bcf-977b-579b-8b15-e3ddf5401153" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-1)\\cdot (x)+(-1)\\cdot (z)+(2)\\cdot (y),$ where $x=t + 3 s$, $y=s - t$, $z=- 3 s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-1)\\cdot (3)+(2)\\cdot (1)+(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-3 + 2 + 3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "537a115e-5710-57f1-ae96-b7d875e20ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546101} {:answer/id #uuid "667c89c6-52b5-528d-a4fb-5278cdbb9d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546104} {:answer/id #uuid "892a708e-7b21-5efd-a84f-5ffafb289617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546115} {:answer/id #uuid "d066addd-c37f-5b9e-9396-55a49b9b63c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546124} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a996ab-78ce-5dae-bfc5-cbbfaefb9e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "537a115e-5710-57f1-ae96-b7d875e20ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546101} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b6b2a4f-ab9a-525f-a4e9-33f7a729e8b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a14e747f-884d-5e7d-bb04-a68302f8fbf5" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-1)\\cdot (y)+(2)\\cdot (x)+(3)\\cdot (z),$ where $x=t - 3 s$, $y=- t - 2 s$, $z=- s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =-3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-2, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(2)\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+(3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-6 + 2 - 3 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28cc858a-bb26-5425-9e3d-889624a9d6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546146} {:answer/id #uuid "c154fa30-500a-5a4e-a923-f15ad6ed70af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28cc858a-bb26-5425-9e3d-889624a9d6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546146} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e378548-8a6e-5c20-a511-23c0a17913af" :answer-field/key "$A(x,y)=\\langle 2x, x^2, 1\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33284fe8-54fa-57ac-b470-9020651b75fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546150} {:answer/id #uuid "f896b200-9766-50e1-bc4b-a192baee38ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f896b200-9766-50e1-bc4b-a192baee38ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546228} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a82c04f-5e96-5b6e-a441-6db69428e37d" :answer-field/key "$B(x,y)=\\langle 2x, x^2, 1\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232572a8-b2de-5eb4-972e-70968de56edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546143} {:answer/id #uuid "d45e3395-7bb4-53b7-8fde-46f8c5fc15d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "232572a8-b2de-5eb4-972e-70968de56edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546143} :answer-field/id #uuid "914737c4-812a-5024-8774-c19a33acea07" :answer-field/key "$C(x,y,z)=\\langle 2x, x^2, 1\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "28d6e948-d7ca-5d96-a5f7-353705699b8e" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^3?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of $\\mathbb R^3.$ A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R^2$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- The function $B(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R^2$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- The function $C(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3$ to a vector in $\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $C(x,y,z)=\\langle 2x, x^2, 1\\rangle$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0184f2ee-4e64-5c2a-8a40-b61e3bd221b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546132} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6d71c8-cb33-5800-aa9d-ea28edf26cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0184f2ee-4e64-5c2a-8a40-b61e3bd221b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546132} :answer-field/id #uuid "057fce